# Which catalog service account may read which Secret Manager secret (roles/secretmanager.secretAccessor, granted on
# that one secret, never project-wide: this project holds other apps' secrets). One line per pair:
#
#   <account> <secret> <need>
#
#   account  web (catalog-web@) or worker (catalog-worker@; the worker service and every catalog Cloud Run job)
#   need     required: the secret must exist and be bound; optional: bound once the secret exists
#
# Read by infra/bootstrap.sh (creates the bindings), infra/deploy.sh (refuses to mount a secret that has no line here)
# and infra/narrow-secret-access.sh (binds these before it removes the project-level grant). A new --set-secrets
# mount needs a line here first; infra/tests/secret-access-manifest.test.mjs fails CI when one is missing.
web     catalog-db-password    required
worker  catalog-db-password    required
worker  openrouter-api-key     required
# M1-F1-R4: the Supabase folder paste on catalog-web (mounted when SUPABASE_FOLDER_PASTE=on).
web     supabase-url           optional
web     supabase-service-key   optional
